# Freeze-critical artifacts -- SE-003.
#
# papers/governance/main_manuscript_freeze_manifest.json pins the SHA-256 of the
# 15 submission files over their RAW BYTES.  Git's end-of-line conversion
# (core.autocrlf, which is machine-local and was `true` on the minting machine)
# rewrote CRLF to LF for five of them on commit, so the committed blobs did not
# match the manifest: the freeze validated 15/15 in the minting worktree but only
# 10/15 at HEAD and 7/15 at the declared anchor.  A reviewer cloning the repo
# could not reproduce the freeze -- which is the paper's reproducibility claim.
#
# `-text` disables all EOL conversion, so git stores and checks out these paths
# byte-for-byte on every platform regardless of the cloner's git configuration.
# Do not replace this with `text eol=...`: that still rewrites bytes on checkout.

papers/main.tex                                 -text
papers/sections/*.tex                           -text
papers/supplementary.tex                        -text
papers/cover_letter.tex                         -text
papers/references.bib                           -text
papers/governance/claims_evidence_matrix.csv    -text
papers/governance/citation_usage_map.csv        -text
papers/governance/artifact_binding.csv          -text
papers/governance/*.json                        -text

# Binary submission artifacts: never diff, never convert.
papers/*.pdf     binary
papers/*.docx    binary
